DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ffcc--mmaattcchh matches _p_a_t_t_e_r_n (empty pattern by default)  using  the  normal
       fontconfig matching rules to find the best font available. If ----ssoorrtt is
       given, the sorted list of best matching fonts is displayed.  The  ----aallll
       option  works like ----ssoorrtt except that no pruning is done on the list of
       fonts.

       If any elements are specified, only those are printed.  Otherwise short
       file  name, family, and style are printed, unless verbose output is re‐
       quested.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       This program follows the usual GNU command line syntax, with  long  op‐
       tions  starting with two dashes (`-'). A summary of options is included
       below.

       --aa     Displays sorted list of best matching fonts, but do not  do  any
              pruning on the list.

       --ss     Displays sorted list of best matching fonts.

       --vv     Print  verbose  output of the whole font pattern for each match,
              or _e_l_e_m_e_n_ts if any is provided.

       --ff     Format output according to the format specifier _f_o_r_m_a_t.

       --VV     Show version of the program and exit.

       --hh     Show summary of options.

       _p_a_t_t_e_r_n
              Displays fonts matching _p_a_t_t_e_r_n (uses empty pattern by default).

       _e_l_e_m_e_n_t
              If set, the _e_l_e_m_e_n_t property is displayed for matching fonts.

